        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Taj Mahal</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1632 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Commissioned by the fifth Mughal emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> (r. 1628–1658); built by more than 20,000 workers and artisans under a board of architects led by Ustad Ahmad Lahori, the court architect, with the chief calligrapher Amanat Khan Shirazi</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">A mausoleum of brick and lime mortar faced with white Makrana marble inlaid with 28 kinds of stone, on a plinth 6 m high, with a dome 23 m high and four minarets over 40 m tall, in a 17-hectare complex with red sandstone buildings and a charbagh garden</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where it is now</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the right bank of the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>; a Monument of National Importance administered by the Archaeological Survey of India</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the tombs of Mumtaz Mahal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a>; its white marble dome and four minarets; pietra dura inlay and Qur'anic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calligraphy">calligraphy</a>; the charbagh garden and reflecting pool; a symbol of love and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>; one of the New 7 Wonders of the World</span></div>
        </div>
