    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> commissioned the Taj Mahal in 1631 as the tomb of Mumtaz Mahal, who died that year giving birth to their 14th child; in 1666 he was buried beside her.</li><li>The mausoleum was completed in 1648 and the whole complex is believed to have been finished in 1653, the work of more than 20,000 workers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> to southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</li><li>Its design draws on Timurid and Mughal tombs such as the Gur-e <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">Amir</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humayuns-tomb">Humayun's Tomb</a>, and its plan and garden are read as an image of paradise.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1942, and again during the India-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> wars of 1965 and 1971, scaffolding was put up around the Taj Mahal to disguise it from bombers.</p></aside>
    </section>

